      "mergeID": "6162272e03e2dd4efde5dea0",
      "mergedPostDetails": "Currently the Microphone Selection is represented by a bunch of checkboxes. This is confusing as checkboxes are usually used for toggling one or more values independently on and off. \nInstead the currently selected microphone should be highlighted by a border and/or some different background and the checkboxes should be removed completely.\n\nAlternatively the checkboxes could be replaced with radio buttons, but then I would recommend to add a \"Confirm\" button, so the user can freely choose a Microphone and then confirm their selection. In that case a radio button would also make sense. However I would still prefer the other option.\n\nRelated Canny:\nhttps://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1137-inconsistent-radio-buttons",
      "mergedPostTitle": "[1137] Microphone selection has confusing UI",
      "parentID": null,
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "6161731b69b7e20fd7384a79",
